Any of you ever play any of the Eye of the Beholder games?

Dungeon Hack is a first person 3d interface just like the EOB's.


You generate your character based on class, alignment, sex, race, and ability
scores (just like AD&D) and then choose a difficulty level (easy, med, hard,
and custom). The game randomly generates the dungeon and plops you down in it.
Very similar to Nethack in the respect that you find unidentified objects
(pink potion, or just an amulet) randomly scattered thruout the dungeon. There
are some puzzles involved in the gameplay too, but nothing _too_ hampering.
Fighting, however is not move-by-move like Nethack, it's more realtime, as
the EOB's.

